# bypass-macs.conf -- devices that bypass tproxy (use CN ISP IP directly)
# Location: /etc/surflare/bypass-macs.conf
# Permissions: chmod 600 (contains device identifiers)
#
# One MAC address per line. Lines starting with # are comments.
# IPs are auto-resolved from /tmp/dhcp.leases on every VPN connect,
# so devices work regardless of DHCP reassignment.
#
# Use cases:
#   - Corporate VPN (AnyConnect etc.): device uses own VPN, not surflare
#   - CN-gated apps (e.g. Thunder/Xunlei): need CN source IP to pass geo-check
#
# Note: On N100/iStoreOS, auto-bypass via DTLS detection (auto_bypass set)
# handles AnyConnect automatically -- no need to add AnyConnect devices here
# unless you want static pre-bypass before DTLS detection fires.
#
# Format: <MAC>   # optional comment
#
# Examples:
# aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff   # work laptop (AnyConnect)
# 11:22:33:44:55:66   # windows-pc (Thunder CN bypass)
